  '[{"ctas":[{"href":"/search?category=playstation-hdmi-repair","label":"Find playstation hdmi port shops"}],"type":"compact_hero","eyebrow":"Repair & Diagnostic Guide","heading":"PlayStation HDMI Port Repair Near You","subtitle":"Compare local independent shops that fix PlayStation & Xbox HDMI ports, review common component failure costs, and find technicians open right now."},{"type":"highlights_strip","items":[{"label":"Typical cost","value":"$75–$160"},{"label":"Turnaround","value":"1–2 days"},{"label":"Common faults","value":"4"}]},{"type":"table_of_contents","title":"On this page"},{"html":"<h2>Is it worth repairing your PlayStation &amp; Xbox HDMI ports?</h2>\n\n<p>Most PlayStation &amp; Xbox HDMI ports that develop faults can be repaired reliably for a fraction of the cost of buying new. Choosing repair preserves working hardware, prevents unnecessary electronic waste, and supports independent local trade technicians.</p>\n<p>However, transparent advice matters: repair stops making financial sense when the main APU processor has suffered silicon fracturing or Southbridge motherboard burns beyond micro-soldering recovery. A professional shop will provide an honest pre-repair assessment before proceeding with work.</p>\n<p>Typical repair costs for PlayStation &amp; Xbox HDMI ports fall within the <strong>$75–$160</strong> range, with standard turnarounds spanning <strong>1–2 days</strong> depending on whether replacement components are in local inventory or require specialist supply ordering.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"type":"feature_grid","items":[{"body":"Blown Panasonic MN864739 / Texas Instruments HDMI retimer transmitter IC or damaged ESD filtering diodes. Micro-soldering replacement of the HDMI encoder chip, filter array inspection, and thermal paste renewal.","title":"White Light of Death (WLOD) — console boots to white light but TV displays ''No Signal''"},{"body":"Tripping over HDMI cables, inserting cords at harsh angles, or aggressive port insertion during relocation. Hot-air desoldering of damaged port, through-hole solder sucker clearing, and precision alignment of new reinforced OEM socket.","title":"Bent, flattened, or missing gold contact pins inside the rear HDMI jack"},{"body":"Excessive lateral force tearing conductive copper pads directly off the top motherboard layer. Micro-wire jumpering using 0.02mm enameled copper wire and ultraviolet (UV) curable solder mask insulation.","title":"Torn micro-copper PCB solder traces from violent cable pulls"},{"body":"Fractured cold solder joints on TMDS high-speed differential signal pins from thermal cycling. Full connector reflow with rosin-flux and silver-bearing lead-free solder alloy.","title":"Display flickers, drops resolution to 480p, or flashes snow-like static artifacts"}],"title":"Common Symptoms & Technical Causes","columns":3},{"html":"<h2>Realistic Repair Costs & Benchmark Pricing</h2>\n<p>The price table below provides verified industry benchmarks for common PlayStation &amp; Xbox HDMI ports repairs. Use these figures to evaluate repair quotes accurately.</p>\n\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Fault / Symptom</th><th>Typical Cost Range</th><th>Bench Turnaround</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody><tr><td><strong>White Light of Death (WLOD) — console boots to white light but TV displays ''No Signal''</strong></td><td>$95–$160</td><td>1–2 days</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Bent, flattened, or missing gold contact pins inside the rear HDMI jack</strong></td><td>$75–$130</td><td>2–4 hours</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Torn micro-copper PCB solder traces from violent cable pulls</strong></td><td>$95–$150</td><td>1–2 days</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Display flickers, drops resolution to 480p, or flashes snow-like static artifacts</strong></td><td>$65–$110</td><td>2 hours</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Factors That Influence Repair Quotes</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Component Quality & Origin:</strong> Genuine OEM parts, certified refurbished original modules, and aftermarket grades differ in cost, color calibration, and durability. Always ask your technician which component tier is quoted.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Component-Level Diagnosis:</strong> Technicians who diagnose and micro-solder specific failed resistors, capacitors, or ports save you significant money compared to shops that simply swap out entire expensive sub-assemblies.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"body":"<ul><li>Eject any physical game discs from the optical drive before packing the console</li><li>Leave external power and HDMI cables at home unless specifically requested by technician</li><li>Perform a PlayStation Plus or USB flash drive save data backup</li></ul>","side":"right","type":"text_image","image":{"alt":"A certified repair technician bench prepared for PlayStation & Xbox HDMI ports","src":"/images/bench.jpg"},"heading":"Preparation Checklist Before Drop-Off"},{"html":"<h2>How to Choose a Reputable Local Repair Shop</h2>\n<p>Before leaving your PlayStation &amp; Xbox HDMI ports with a repair shop, ask these four critical questions:</p>\n<h3>1. What warranty do you provide on parts and labor?</h3>\n<p>Reputable independent repair shops typically offer a 90-day to 1-year written warranty covering both replacement components and bench labor.</p>\n<h3>2. Do you perform diagnostics before charging?</h3>\n<p>Clear diagnostic estimates ensure you are never surprised by unexpected fees. Ask whether initial bench assessment fees apply toward the final repair cost.</p>\n<h3>3. What is your data security policy?</h3>\n<p>For electronic devices storing personal information, ensure the shop has strict confidentiality protocols, does not require unnecessary passwords, and never wipes storage drives without your prior authorization.</p>\n<h3>4. Are turnaround estimates realistic?</h3>\n<p>Confirm whether common parts are on the shelf or need to be ordered, so you have an accurate timeline for pickup.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"type":"faq_accordion","items":[{"answer":"Most standard repairs range between $75–$160, depending on component availability and whether the fault is a modular replacement or micro-soldering.","question":"How much does playstation hdmi port repair typically cost?"},{"answer":"Blown Panasonic MN864739 / Texas Instruments HDMI retimer transmitter IC or damaged ESD filtering diodes. Micro-soldering replacement of the HDMI encoder chip, filter array inspection, and thermal paste renewal. Expect typical costs around $95–$160 with turnaround of 1–2 days.","question":"How is ''White Light of Death (WLOD) — console boots to white light but TV displays ''No Signal'''' fixed?"},{"answer":"Most jobs are completed within 1–2 days. In-stock modular repairs are frequently finished the same day.","question":"How long will the repair take?"},{"answer":"Consider replacement when the main APU processor has suffered silicon fracturing or Southbridge motherboard burns beyond micro-soldering recovery.","question":"When should I replace rather than repair?"},{"answer":"Under Right to Repair laws in many jurisdictions, third-party repairs do not void manufacturer warranties unless the repair itself directly causes damage to other components.","question":"Does third-party repair void my manufacturer warranty?"},{"answer":"While many shops accept walk-ins, calling ahead or booking online ensures replacement parts are reserved and technician bench time is scheduled immediately.","question":"Do I need to book an appointment in advance?"}],"title":"Frequently Asked Questions"},{"cta":{"href":"/search?category=playstation-hdmi-repair","label":"Search the local directory"},"body":"Filter by active opening hours, on-site home visits, collection service, and transparent part warranties.","tone":"signal","type":"cta_banner","heading":"Find a verified playstation hdmi port expert near you"}]'::jsonb,
