  array['power-tools repair', 'power-tools repair near me', 'power-tools repair in mumbai', 'power-tools repair cost', 'fix power tools', 'power tools repair technician', 'local power-tools service'],
  '[{"ctas":[{"href":"/search?category=power-tools","label":"Find power tools & workshop equipment shops"}],"type":"compact_hero","eyebrow":"Repair & Diagnostic Guide","heading":"Power Tools & Workshop Equipment Near You","subtitle":"Compare local independent shops that fix power tools, review common component failure costs, and find technicians open right now."},{"type":"highlights_strip","items":[{"label":"Typical cost","value":"$40–$220"},{"label":"Turnaround","value":"1–5 days"},{"label":"Common faults","value":"5"}]},{"type":"table_of_contents","title":"On this page"},{"html":"<h2>Is it worth repairing your power tools?</h2>\n\n<p>Most power tools that develop faults can be repaired reliably for a fraction of the cost of buying new. Choosing repair preserves working hardware, prevents unnecessary electronic waste, and supports independent local trade technicians.</p>\n<p>However, transparent advice matters: repair stops making financial sense when motor armature windings have experienced complete catastrophic burnout melting internal plastic housing. A professional shop will provide an honest pre-repair assessment before proceeding with work.</p>\n<p>Typical repair costs for power tools fall within the <strong>$40–$220</strong> range, with standard turnarounds spanning <strong>1–5 days</strong> depending on whether replacement components are in local inventory or require specialist supply ordering.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"type":"feature_grid","items":[{"body":"Worn carbon brushes sparking against dirty or pitted commutator bars. Carbon brush set replacement and commutator copper bar polishing/undercutting.","title":"Tool sparks heavily from vents, smells like burning ozone, runs weak"},{"body":"Worn chuck jaws, damaged spindle bearings, or stripped planetary gearbox gears. Keyless chuck replacement and gearbox greasing.","title":"Cordless drill / impact driver chuck wobbles or will not grip bits"},{"body":"Fine sawdust infiltrating the variable speed trigger potentiometer and switch contacts. Sealed trigger switch replacement and wiring harness inspection.","title":"Tool trigger switch intermittent or variable speed not working"},{"body":"Individual cell group voltage imbalance tripping low-voltage lock on pack BMS. BMS diagnostic, cell group bench rebalancing, or individual cell group spot-welding replacement.","title":"Power tool lithium battery pack blinks error code and will not charge"},{"body":"Worn high-RPM spindle bearings or bent arbor flange. Spindle bearing extraction and replacement with precision sealed bearings.","title":"Miter saw / table saw blade arbor vibrating heavily"}],"title":"Common Symptoms & Technical Causes","columns":3},{"html":"<h2>Realistic Repair Costs & Benchmark Pricing</h2>\n<p>The price table below provides verified industry benchmarks for common power tools repairs. Use these figures to evaluate repair quotes accurately.</p>\n\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Fault / Symptom</th><th>Typical Cost Range</th><th>Bench Turnaround</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody><tr><td><strong>Tool sparks heavily from vents, smells like burning ozone, runs weak</strong></td><td>$35–$75</td><td>same day to 1 day</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cordless drill / impact driver chuck wobbles or will not grip bits</strong></td><td>$45–$95</td><td>1–2 days</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Tool trigger switch intermittent or variable speed not working</strong></td><td>$40–$85</td><td>1–2 days</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Power tool lithium battery pack blinks error code and will not charge</strong></td><td>$45–$110</td><td>1–3 days</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Miter saw / table saw blade arbor vibrating heavily</strong></td><td>$60–$140</td><td>2–4 days</td></tr></tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Factors That Influence Repair Quotes</h3>\n<p><strong>1. Component Quality & Origin:</strong> Genuine OEM parts, certified refurbished original modules, and aftermarket grades differ in cost, color calibration, and durability. Always ask your technician which component tier is quoted.</p>\n<p><strong>2. Component-Level Diagnosis:</strong> Technicians who diagnose and micro-solder specific failed resistors, capacitors, or ports save you significant money compared to shops that simply swap out entire expensive sub-assemblies.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"body":"<ul><li>Wipe heavy sawdust or grease from exterior tool body</li><li>Bring the corresponding battery and charger for cordless tool diagnosis</li><li>Remove saw blades or router bits before bringing tools to the shop</li></ul>","side":"right","type":"text_image","image":{"alt":"A certified repair technician bench prepared for power tools","src":"/images/bench.jpg"},"heading":"Preparation Checklist Before Drop-Off"},{"html":"<h2>How to Choose a Reputable Local Repair Shop</h2>\n<p>Before leaving your power tools with a repair shop, ask these four critical questions:</p>\n<h3>1. What warranty do you provide on parts and labor?</h3>\n<p>Reputable independent repair shops typically offer a 90-day to 1-year written warranty covering both replacement components and bench labor.</p>\n<h3>2. Do you perform diagnostics before charging?</h3>\n<p>Clear diagnostic estimates ensure you are never surprised by unexpected fees. Ask whether initial bench assessment fees apply toward the final repair cost.</p>\n<h3>3. What is your data security policy?</h3>\n<p>For electronic devices storing personal information, ensure the shop has strict confidentiality protocols, does not require unnecessary passwords, and never wipes storage drives without your prior authorization.</p>\n<h3>4. Are turnaround estimates realistic?</h3>\n<p>Confirm whether common parts are on the shelf or need to be ordered, so you have an accurate timeline for pickup.</p>","type":"rich_text","width":"prose"},{"type":"faq_accordion","items":[{"answer":"Most standard repairs range between $40–$220, depending on component availability and whether the fault is a modular replacement or micro-soldering.","question":"How much does power tools & workshop equipment typically cost?"},{"answer":"Worn carbon brushes sparking against dirty or pitted commutator bars. Carbon brush set replacement and commutator copper bar polishing/undercutting. Expect typical costs around $35–$75 with turnaround of same day to 1 day.","question":"How is ''Tool sparks heavily from vents, smells like burning ozone, runs weak'' fixed?"},{"answer":"Most jobs are completed within 1–5 days. In-stock modular repairs are frequently finished the same day.","question":"How long will the repair take?"},{"answer":"Consider replacement when motor armature windings have experienced complete catastrophic burnout melting internal plastic housing.","question":"When should I replace rather than repair?"},{"answer":"Under Right to Repair laws in many jurisdictions, third-party repairs do not void manufacturer warranties unless the repair itself directly causes damage to other components.","question":"Does third-party repair void my manufacturer warranty?"},{"answer":"While many shops accept walk-ins, calling ahead or booking online ensures replacement parts are reserved and technician bench time is scheduled immediately.","question":"Do I need to book an appointment in advance?"}],"title":"Frequently Asked Questions"},{"cta":{"href":"/search?category=power-tools","label":"Search the local directory"},"body":"Filter by active opening hours, on-site home visits, collection service, and transparent part warranties.","tone":"signal","type":"cta_banner","heading":"Find a verified power tools & workshop equipment expert near you"}]'::jsonb,
